# Build context for this image is the REPO ROOT (docker-compose.yml sets
# `context: ../..`), not services/orion-hub/. That is what broke the previous
# version of this file, which read:
#
#     *
#     !ai-voice-service/**
#     !orion-bus/client/**
#
# Those two re-includes are paths under `services/`, so they match nothing at
# the repo root -- leaving `*` to exclude the ENTIRE context. BuildKit then
# hashes an effectively empty context, so every `COPY` in the Dockerfile
# (orion, services/orion-hub, requirements) stayed pinned to whatever layer was
# cached first and NO code change could reach the image again. Confirmed live
# 2026-09-03: `COPY orion /app/orion` reported CACHED across repeated
# --build deploys while the running container served a copy of
# turn_orchestrator.py hours older than the source; removing this file made the
# same build re-run that COPY and pick the change up immediately.
#
# So: exclude by path, and never with a bare `*`. Anything the Dockerfile
# COPYs must NOT be listed here.

# VCS + local agent scratch
.git
.worktrees
.claude/worktrees

# Virtualenvs and caches (orion_dev alone is GBs)
orion_dev
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Generated knowledge-graph artifacts (graph.json alone is ~43MB)
graphify-out

# Vendored JS trees
**/node_modules
services/orion-ai-town/upstream

# Model weights and large local data
**/*.gguf
**/*.safetensors
**/*.bin

# Secrets -- never in an image layer
**/.env
